 "description": "<p><span style='font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,sans-serif;'>Peel Region, together with our contractor, have created this map. It lets residents of Peel Region search their address and see when and where downspout surveys are happening in their community. Active testing is ongoing from spring through fall. During active seasons, the map will be updated on a daily basis.</span></p><p><span style='font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,sans-serif;'>&nbsp;A downspout is a vertical pipe on the outside of your home that carried rainwater from the roof to the ground. Some downspouts drain directly to your lawn, while others go directly into the ground, where it may be draining water into the sanitary sewer system. During heavy rainstorms, rainwater entering the sanitary sewer system can add extra water and increase the risk of flooding. Downspout Survey's are the first step of Peel Region's Downspout Disconnection Program, a simple inspection to see where downspouts are draining. This program helps reduce the risk of flooding by finding stormwater that may be leaking into the sanitary sewer system which might cause it to overflow.</span></p><p><span style='font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,sans-serif;'>Downspouts found connected to the sanitary sewer will be identified and only those property owners will be contacted to participate in the Peel Region’s Downspout Disconnection Program, which completes disconnections of downspouts for residents. &nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style='font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,sans-serif;'>The Program is rolled out on a neighbourhood-by-neighbourhood basis (called blocks). Blocks with higher priority naturally are started earlier. Blocks are prioritized based on the history of flooding, overflows of sewers to the environment, and sanitary sewer capacity limitations.&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style='font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,sans-serif;'>For more information on downspout surveys visit </span><a target='_blank' href='https://peelregion.ca/water/pipes-downspouts/downspouts/downspout-surveys' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'><span style='font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,sans-serif;'>Downspout surveys - peelregion.ca</span></a><span style='font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,sans-serif;'>. For more information on disconnecting a downspout visit </span><a target='_blank' href='https://peelregion.ca/water/pipes-downspouts/downspouts/disconnecting-downspout' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'><span style='font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:12.0pt;'><span style='line-height:115%;'>Disconnecting a downspout - peelregion.ca</span></span></a><span style='font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:12.0pt;'><span style='line-height:115%;'> or call Peel Region at 905-791-7800, ext. 4409.</span></span></p><p><strong>We appreciate your feedback on our Map. Please send any comments or suggestions to Michelle Skerlan at </strong><a href='mailto:michelle.skerlan@peelregion.ca' rel='nofollow ugc'><strong>michelle.skerlan@peelregion.ca</strong></a><strong>.</strong></p>",
 "tags": [
